### **The first 30 seconds**

The experience must be deliberately engineered.

1. User opens Kea Parrot.
2. Immediately sees interesting public content.
3. Can participate in a poll or play a game without a complicated registration process, within the 60-minute guest participation window (see Guest Session Rule below).
4. When they want to post, save or follow something, they can create an account.
5. They discover that more interesting activities are happening around them.

I strongly recommend allowing limited guest browsing and guest participation, under the Guest Session Rule below.

**Guest Session Rule (D-03, canonical — owner decision 2026-11-20).** A guest is an unauthenticated visitor, identified by a server-issued guest-session token stored in the browser. A guest is NOT an account. A guest MAY: browse public discovery; view polls/results and game descriptions; vote in polls; play the 3 games. A guest may NOT: post, comment, react, join communities, report content, or create any game record associated with an account. (Guest game sessions are tied to the guest session only, never to an account.) LIMITED TIME: a guest participation window lasts **60 minutes from the guest session's first vote or game start**, and ends on browser close, whichever is first. After expiry the guest must register / log in to vote or play again. One vote per poll per guest session. Guest votes are counted. Guest game scores are not saved to a profile and do not appear on leaderboards. After registration, guest-session votes/scores do NOT transfer to the new account (no merge in MVP). Rate limits apply per guest session + IP (thresholds TBD in Product P1 config — do not invent). Guests may NOT change/remove a vote.

Don't make account registration the price of admission.

