# **PART 2 — COMPETITIVE POSITIONING**

## **4. Understand the market you are entering**

Kea Parrot will compete with several categories rather than one direct competitor.

| Platform  | What it does well                        | Opportunity for Kea Parrot                                               |
| --------- | ---------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| Reddit    | Topic-based communities and discussions  | Make participation more immediate and contextual                     |
| Snapchat  | Social interaction and location features | Make discovery possible without an existing social graph             |
| TikTok    | Entertainment and content discovery      | Offer interactive rather than predominantly passive experiences      |
| Discord   | Live communities and group interaction   | Remove the need to join established servers                          |
| Nextdoor  | Neighbourhood communities                | Add games, instant polls and lightweight entertainment               |
| Yik Yak   | Anonymous campus conversations           | Expand into games, discovery and global participation                |
| GeoGuessr | Location-based competitive entertainment | Introduce lightweight social exploration and user-created challenges |

These are adjacent competitors, not identical products.

### **Your competitive advantage**

I would build Kea Parrot around five differentiators.

**1. No social graph required**

Users don't need to follow 50 people before the product becomes interesting.

**2. Immediate participation**

A user can vote, react, play or discover something almost immediately.

**3. Physical + digital discovery**

The platform connects local activity with global entertainment.

**4. User-generated experiences**

Users don't just publish content. They create activities other people can participate in.

**5. Cross-community interaction**

Universities, cities, event communities and interest groups can participate in the same platform.

### **The competitive positioning statement**

I would use this internally:

> Kea Parrot is the instant social discovery platform that combines real-time community activity, anonymous participation, location-aware discovery and bite-sized entertainment into one accessible experience.

Don't market it as a TikTok competitor, a Reddit competitor or a gaming platform.

Create a category around the combination.

## **5. Your competitive moat**

Features alone are not a moat. Competitors can copy features.

Your long-term advantage needs to come from four assets:

**A. Activity density**

The number of interesting activities happening in a particular community at any given time.

**B. Community graph**

Relationships between users, communities, locations, interests and recurring activities.

**C. Creator ecosystem**

People who consistently create interesting polls, challenges, mysteries and experiences.

**D. Activity intelligence**

An understanding of which experiences generate meaningful participation, repeat visits and positive community outcomes.

Eventually, Kea Parrot should become better at presenting the right activity to the right person at the right time.

That is much harder to replicate than a simple anonymous posting feature.

