The data model is one of the most important decisions because Kea Parrot will eventually have large volumes of user-generated content and interactions.

I recommend these foundational entities:

| Table              | Purpose                                   |
| ------------------ | ----------------------------------------- |
| users              | Authentication identity                   |
| profiles           | Public user profiles                      |
| communities        | University, city and interest communities |
| community_members  | Community membership                      |
| posts              | Notes, questions and discussions          |
| post_reactions     | Likes and reactions                       |
| comments           | Discussions under posts                   |
| polls              | Poll configuration                        |
| poll_options       | Available answers                         |
| poll_votes         | User voting records                       |
| games              | Game definitions                          |
| game_sessions      | Individual game attempts                  |
| challenges         | User-created challenges                   |
| challenge_entries  | Participation records                     |
| locations          | Publicly discoverable location entities   |
| location_drops     | Location-based content                    |
| notifications      | User notifications                        |
| reports            | Moderation reports                        |
| moderation_actions | Enforcement records                       |
| achievements       | Achievement definitions                   |
| user_achievements  | Earned achievements                       |
| subscriptions      | Paid membership                           |
| ad_campaigns       | Sponsored experiences                     |
| analytics_events   | Product analytics                         |

### **Five database decisions I would insist on**

**1. Anonymous does not mean unaccountable.**

Separate public identity from internal account identity.

A user can publish anonymously, but the platform retains the internal account reference for moderation and enforcement.

**2. Location must be privacy-conscious.**

Use approximate location or geospatial cells for discovery. Avoid exposing raw GPS coordinates or exact real-time user positions.

**3. Votes must be transaction-safe.**

A user must not be able to vote multiple times on a single-vote poll by exploiting simultaneous requests.

Use database constraints and transactions.

**4. MVP posts are persistent; no expiry infrastructure in Product P1.**

MVP posts are persistent unless removed by their owner or moderation action. Content expiry is designed in Product P2 with temporary content (see KEA-PRD-001 §9.6). Do not build expiry timestamps or background cleanup processes in Product P1.

**5. Never rely exclusively on client-side security.**

Authorization, rate limits, validation and sensitive business rules must be enforced server-side.

## **9. Real-time architecture**

This is critical because Kea Parrot's identity depends on immediate interaction.

When someone votes in a poll, other participants should see the results update without refreshing.

Social rooms: unscoped idea — no requirements; do not build (removed 2026-11-20).

When a challenge expires, it should disappear or transition to its completed state.

I recommend separating three types of realtime communication:

| Mechanism            | Use                            |
| -------------------- | ------------------------------ |
| Database persistence | Permanent records              |
| Broadcast            | Live events and updates        |
| Presence             | Temporary online participation |

Supabase's documentation recommends Broadcast over Postgres Changes for more scalable realtime fan-out. Its guidance also explains that Postgres Changes can become expensive when many subscribers receive each change.&#x20;

[image](https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=https://supabase.com\&sz=32)

Supabase Docs+2



Do not broadcast every database operation to every connected user.

Use targeted channels, authorization and event filtering.

