# **PART 7 — GO-TO-MARKET AND USER ACQUISITION**

## **18. Everyone is the eventual audience, but don't launch everywhere**

This is a crucial distinction.

Your product can be designed for everyone without trying to acquire everyone on day one.

I recommend a **concentrated-community launch strategy**.

Start in Ghana, establish a successful community, then expand across other markets.

Why Ghana?

- You can conduct direct user research.
- You can organize physical launch campaigns.
- Universities provide concentrated communities.
- You can approach local businesses directly.
- You can test pricing and business partnerships.
- You can learn from real users before spending heavily on international acquisition.

The initial audience is a distribution strategy, not a permanent restriction on who can use Kea Parrot.

